ups before its closing figure, where the edition has seven, and that fixes the start. Bar 6 is cut off after the D–C# 8ths, which fixes the end. The cramped beams and ledger lines make exact pitches hard to read. Seeing the next line, or a higher-resolution scan, would make the bar 6 cut-off certain."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6063,"cache_read_input_tokens":751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6063},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"205afd23-40d3-4b32-9eb7-a21a688cb614","uuid":"c3ed2a5f-b5d3-4e21-9373-043ef9ea9fe0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:56:43.139Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj2di7QgX4mVRnDmd4Tb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01C4zSi4YvdPvFKawLfW2o8P":{"working":"The line opens with a clef and three sharps but no time signature, which fits a line that starts mid-movement. Before the first barline (about x=375) there are only three groups of four 32nds (low note, then the upper octave three times). After them comes the closing figure: a grace note, a 16th, then two 32nds. That closing figure is the end of bar 1 (grace B5, A5, G#5, F#5). Bar 1 has seven such groups, so the line starts on its last three, roughly (C#5 C#6…), (B4 B5…), (A4 A5 G#5 A5). The first four groups are on the previous line.\n\nNext stretch (to about x=690): a grace + 16th + two 32nds figure, twice; then two 8ths (A4, G#4); a dotted figure with a slur; a quarter; then two 16ths marked p. That is bar 2.\n\nNext stretch (to about x=920): grace, 8th, two 16ths, two 8ths, a dotted 8th + 16th under a slur, an 8th, two 16ths. That is bar 3.\n\nNext stretch (to about x=1225): the same pattern ending in four 32nds, marked cresc. That is bar 4.\n\nNext, a long stretch